# A helper that reads under a key handed in, called with the key written at the call, outside of loops. The time is spent in the helper's own loop. The call was left as a call, and in the helper the key is any text: a record
# of seven names is over what is told apart by names, so the read stayed generic. Now the helper is copied in line at such a call where what is held of the holder under the key says layouts: in the copy the key is a
# constant and the read goes by name, whatever the number and the kinds of the fields.
# RUN: walk f2 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f2:Body
# CHECK-NOT: CallDirect
# CHECK: GetSlot {{*}} key="age"
# CHECK-NOT: CallDirect
# CHECK: GetSlot {{*}} key="zip"
# CHECK-NOT: CallDirect
